      "inspected_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor": "The selected do! method removes incoming edges and returns the graph; it does not evaluate an intervention distribution.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "Adjustment and frontdoor methods expose mandatory I and allowed R sets; default R contains every nonendpoint vertex. The example explicitly removes unobserved vertices.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "Find methods return sets or false; iterator exhaustion is nothing and iterator size is unknown. Empty solution and no emitted solutions must stay distinct.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "find_backdoor_adjustment passes find_covariate_adjustment directly to setdiff without a local false guard; exact failure behavior remains a native conformance question.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "Selected frontdoor search is a graphical set search, not a general ID/IDC or counterfactual evaluator.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "The recanting-witness helper describes a path-specific question under complete observations. Its named proof is not inspected in this review.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "Inspected tests include explicit allowed-set exclusions, expected set enumeration, false results and selected invalid d-separation inputs. Tests were not executed.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        },
        {
          "anchor": "Project metadata declares version 0.19.4 with dependency ranges; the selected license declares MIT. Neither binds a fully resolved runtime distribution.",
          "inspection": "Selected original source path"
        }
